    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1 range 1', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map address-family ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent for the Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid index 1 range 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command assigns a static SID (Segment ID) with value ::1 and marks it as an End SID (used for node segments).\\n- In Cisco, the equivalent is setting a prefix-SID index (equivalent to the SID value) with a range of 1 (for a single segment).\\n- The `index 1` corresponds to the Huawei ::1 value (assuming the base value is ::0), and the functionality is the same (creates a node segment).\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1 range 1'}]]": 1,
